      "writtenOn": "2024-04-04T17:13:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These functions (circle and rrect too), will need to go inside the `if (layer)` check so that any image filter on the paint is handled first. The `PredrawFlags::kSkipMaskFilterAutoLayer` should be passed in so the mask filter is not converted to an image filter yet.\n\nInside the `if (layer)`, if drawRectBlurMaskFilter() returns false but there is a mask filter, then we need to make a new `AutoLayerForImageFilter` directly and  pass in `skipMaskFilterLayer\u003dtrue`. For the time being we could wrap all this extra logic in a call to `device-\u003euseDrawCoverageMaskForMaskFilters()` since this direct analytic blurring is a component of the long-term implementation. \n\nIt\u0027s not necessarily feasible, but if the `drawRectBlurMaskFilter()` function always succeeds when it fully implemented and the SkCanvas is responsible for detecting when that\u0027s possible, the flow is hopefully simpler.  In that world, SkCanvas was pre-determine that the blur can be analytic, and add the `kSkipMaskFilterAutoLayer` flag to `aboutToDraw()`. Then within the `if(layer)` it either calls `drawRect()` or `drawRectBlurMaskFilter()` but doesn\u0027t have to worry about falling back from the analytic blur to an image-based blur.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2278,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2281,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6361dc56d6025355244bfa40a4ec192f166a4570",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
