      "writtenOn": "2024-04-04T17:13:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know this device-space restriction was inherited from Ganesh, but is there a chance we can structure the graphite code and effect so that we can render it in local space?\n\nThat would simplify this function and also make it (hopefully) not need to be an optional constructor that can fail.\n\nLooking at the shader code very quickly, I\u0027d think that we could update the logic to render under an arbitrary transform so long as the integral table had sufficient resolution to match the sampling rate in device space.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6361dc56d6025355244bfa40a4ec192f166a4570",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
